RESULTS

axe, light theme (default + full 2.2AA tag set): 0 violations, 0 incomplete,
38-39 passes.

axe, dark theme (`class="dark"` on <html>, matching the app's real dark-mode
toggle mechanism — confirmed the compiled CSS uses `.dark\:text-*:is(.dark *)`
selectors, i.e. class-strategy, not media-query): 1 violation —
`color-contrast`, serious, 65 nodes. INVESTIGATED and ATTRIBUTED per
procedure point 5:
  - The flagged nodes are `h5`, `strong` (the big dollar figure), several
    `<p class="mt-1/mt-2/mt-3">` evidence lines, the "Inspect evidence"
    buttons, the frontier `<th>`/`<td>` cells and frontier section headings
    — i.e. every element in `whatif-spending-option` and
    `whatif-spending-frontier` that carries NO `dark:text-*` class at all
    (only specific muted lines use `text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300`).
    Confirmed via computed style: color is plain black (`rgb(0,0,0)`,
    browser default, since `body{line-height:inherit;margin:0}` sets no
    color and no ancestor in base.html/guardrails.html sets one either) on
    a dark card background — invisible in dark mode.
  - `[data-spending-apply="current"]` (the NEW Apply button/form this task
    added to the Current card) is ABSENT from the violation list in both
    themes. Its markup (`bg-accent-strong ... text-white`) uses
    `--accent-strong: 79 70 229` (indigo-600), which `styles.css` documents
    as "theme-invariant" — same value inside and outside `.dark`. Computed
    contrast in both themes: white (L=1.0) vs rgb(79,70,229) (L≈0.117) →
    ≈6.29:1, clearing the 4.5:1 text threshold (point 7) with margin, in
    BOTH themes (point 12 parity) — confirmed by axe AND by hand
    calculation AND by getComputedStyle.
  - Per procedure point 5, I attribute rather than fail: every flagged node
    sits on markup BYTE-IDENTICAL to master (base d6c554f) — this
    `whatif-spending-option`/`whatif-spending-frontier` template renders
    identically for the Current card, the two Headline cards
    (planned-8500/flex-9000, already shipping in production today), and
    both frontier tables. The ONLY line this task changed is the one
    sentence quoted above, which is itself `text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300`
    and correctly NOT in the violation list. This is a PRE-EXISTING,
    site-wide dark-mode contrast defect in this component (present on every
    already-deployed card and frontier row), not something CP1 introduced
    or replicated into new content — CP1 only added the identical Apply
    button pattern already used (and already contrast-clean) elsewhere, and
    reused the surrounding text nodes verbatim. Filed as a NOTE below, not a
    FAIL, per the checker's scope rule ("FAIL only ... this task's change
    introduced or replicated into new content").

MANUAL CHECKS (acceptance criterion 7)

- Keyboard reachability: `<button type="submit" data-spending-apply="current">`
  inside `<form data-spending-apply-form>`, a plain focusable native button;
  no tabindex tricks. Confirmed programmatically: focusing the card's
  "Inspect evidence" button and pressing Tab moves `document.activeElement`
  to the new Apply button next in DOM/visual order (`flex flex-wrap gap-2`
  siblings) — matches point 9 (focus order follows visual order).
- Visible focus indicator: computed style on focus = `outline: solid 2px,
  offset 2px`, color `rgb(79,70,229)` (light) / `rgb(165,180,252)` (dark) —
  identical `focus:outline focus:outline-2 focus:outline-offset-2
  focus:outline-accent` class already used by every sibling Apply/Inspect
  button (the sitewide focus-ring token from the prior backlog-a11y-2 run).
  Non-text contrast of the ring against its card background: ≈6.3:1 (light),
  ≈7.6:1 (dark) — clears the ≥3:1 UI-boundary bar in point 7, in both
  themes (point 12).
- Colour contrast of the button itself: see axe results above — passes both
  themes, ≈6.29:1.
- Target size: axe's `target-size` rule is present but disabled by default
  in this axe-core version; measured directly instead —
  `boundingBox()` = 160.4×42.5 CSS px, far above the 24×24 minimum (WCAG
  2.2 SC 2.5.8 / point 7's spirit), same padding classes (`px-3 py-2`) as
  every sibling Apply button already in production.
- No duplicate IDs / nested forms: the new `<form data-spending-apply-form>`
  has no `id` attribute (matches siblings, which key off `data-*` not
  `id`); it sits inside `<div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">` inside
  `<article>`, never inside another `<form>` — confirmed the enclosing
  `#spending-optimizer-form` in `spending_optimizer.html` closes (`</form>`
  line 94) well before `#spending-optimizer-results` (line 107) opens, so
  the results partial (and this new form) is never a `<form>` descendant.
  axe's `duplicate-id`/`duplicate-id-aria` rules: 0 violations in both
  themes, both tag sets.
- Enumerated surfaces per the brief: read `buildSpendingOptimizerView` in
  `internal/handlers/whatif/handlers_spending_optimizer.go` — candidates are
  routed by an exclusive `switch { case c.Baseline: view.Current = ...;
  case c.Kind=="planned": view.PlannedRows ...; case c.Kind=="flexible":
  view.FlexibleRows ...}`, so the current/baseline candidate can NEVER also
  land in a frontier slice. Confirmed empirically in the audit fixture body
  (`data-spending-apply="current"` appears exactly once; no
  `data-spending-row="current"` anywhere) and this is additionally pinned by
  the task's own new test `TestSpendingOptimizerRenderCurrentPlanApply`,
  which asserts the same thing across qualifying/non-qualifying states. No
  duplicate control introduced.
- Heading/landmark structure: unchanged — `h4[data-spending-outcome]` >
  `h5` (card titles) / `h5#{kind}-frontier-heading` (frontier section
  titles), same as master; the parent chain is h1 > h2 "Spending plan" > h3
  "How much can I spend?" (all pre-existing, outside this diff). axe's
  `heading-order`/`landmark-*`/`page-has-heading-one` rules: 0 violations.
- Reworded sentence: "Failed rows remain available for graph inspection
  only." reads correctly and is now ACCURATE — previously the Current card
  could never get an Apply token (pre-CP1 rule excluded `Baseline`
